{
  "slug": "heimdall",
  "name": "Heimdall",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Analyze video files: especially bug report screen recordings, directly in Claude Code. Extracts frames via ffmpeg, transcribes audio via whisper-cpp, and produces structured reports with steps-to-reproduce, error messages, and timestamps. All heavy work runs in a subagent so your main context stays clean.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills**, **1 agent**, **2 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `setup-deps` (Install heimdall dependencies (ffmpeg, whisper-cpp, whisper model)), `video-watching` (Analyzes video files when the user mentions a video file path in conversation), `watch` (Analyze a video file — extract frames, transcribe audio, produce a structured report)\n- **Agents** (1): `heimdall` (Analyzes video files by extracting frames and audio transcripts, then producing structured reports)\n- **Commands** (2): `setup` (Install heimdall dependencies (ffmpeg, whisper-cpp)), `watch` (Analyze a video file — extract frames, transcribe audio, produce a structured report)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install heimdall@claude-community` from `pranavtotla/heimdall`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
